      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the patch stays, could the P3S parts go into P3S headers, as `vma_pte_add_slice()` does in `mm/p3s/pgtable.h`? `do_swap_page()` and `unuse_pte()` would then keep a one-line call instead of an `#ifdef` block each. With no-op fallbacks (e.g. in `\u003clinux/p3s/swap.h\u003e`), `include/linux/swapops.h` and `mm/internal.h` wouldn\u0027t need `#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` either. And `try_to_unmap_one()` could use `vma_slice_offset(vma, address)` rather than `(pte_val(pteval) \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB) \u0026 3`.",
